<title>BELGIUM: Generale Bank to become Belfox clearer.</title>
<headline>Generale Bank to become Belfox clearer.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium's largest bank, Generale Bank, said on Wednesday it had decided to become a General Clearing Member of the Belfox futures and options exchange from October 1.</p>
<p>A General Clearing Member is authorised to act as a counterparty in trades executed for its own account or the account of its own clients as well as trades executed for the account of other members or for the account of clients in the books of other members.</p>
<p>Other General Clearing Members are  Bank Degroof and Kredietbank.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810.</p>
</text>
